# 🧠 Important Java Keywords

## `this`

Refers to the current object.

```java
this.name = name;
```

The left-hand `this.name` is the instance variable. The right-hand `name` is the constructor parameter.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## `this()`

Calls another constructor in the same class.

```java
Student() {
    this("Unknown");
}
```

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## Constructor vs. Method

| Feature | Constructor | Method |
|---|---|---|
| Name | Same as class | Any valid method name |
| Return type | No return type | Has a return type or `void` |
| Purpose | Initialize an object | Perform an operation |
| Called | During object creation | When invoked |
| Overloading | Yes | Yes |

